---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Section from "../components/Section.astro";
import { siteConfig, PRIVACY_POLICY_VERSION } from "../lib/config";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description={`How ${siteConfig.name} collects, uses, and protects your information.`}>
  <Section title="Privacy Policy">
    <div class="prose prose-neutral max-w-none dark:prose-invert">
      <p class="rounded-md border border-amber-300 bg-amber-50 p-4 text-sm text-amber-900 not-prose dark:border-amber-700 dark:bg-amber-950 dark:text-amber-100">
        <strong>Draft notice:</strong> this policy (version {PRIVACY_POLICY_VERSION}) describes the data practices implemented in this
        website as built. It is written to align with general good-practice principles and the Nigeria Data Protection Act
        (NDPA) 2023 framework, but it has <strong>not</strong> been reviewed by a qualified lawyer. Obtain legal review before
        relying on this as your community's final privacy policy, especially the sections on legal basis, data
        subject rights, and cross-border transfer (e.g. if Supabase infrastructure is hosted outside Nigeria).
      </p>

      <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {siteConfig.name} ("we", "us", "the community") operates this website to organise community activities and
        maintain a directory of members who choose to participate publicly. Contact: {siteConfig.contactEmail}.
      </p>

      <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Registration data:</strong> display name, email, optional full name, skills, interests, learning goals, experience level, career stage, location, and optional professional links, collected via the Join form.</li>
        <li><strong>Public profile data:</strong> only the subset of registration data you explicitly opt into showing publicly, and only once an administrator approves publication.</li>
        <li><strong>Achievement and spotlight data:</strong> details you or a nominator submit about an achievement, used only with your consent.</li>
        <li><strong>Content submissions:</strong> project and content submissions you choose to share for editorial review.</li>
        <li><strong>Contact messages:</strong> information you submit through the Contact form.</li>
        <li><strong>Consent records:</strong> a history of what you agreed to and when, including withdrawals.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Why we process it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To review and manage your community membership.</li>
        <li>To operate the public member directory and spotlight features, strictly according to your visibility choices.</li>
        <li>To organise and communicate about events, learning groups, and relevant opportunities, where you have consented to non-essential communications.</li>
        <li>To maintain the integrity and security of the website and prevent abuse.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>4. Your visibility choices</h2>
      <p>
        Directory listing, spotlight publication, and non-essential communications are tracked as separate, optional
        consents. Your email address, full legal name, and any administrator notes are never shown publicly, and are
        never included in member directory responses or public API output, regardless of your visibility settings.
      </p>

      <h2>5. Who can see your information</h2>
      <p>
        Your private information (email, full name, admin notes) is visible only to authorised community
        administrators via a protected admin area, enforced by database-level access rules — not merely by hiding
        buttons in the website design. Public profile fields are visible to anyone visiting the website only after
        both your consent and administrator approval.
      </p>

      <h2>6. Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        We retain membership and consent records for as long as you are an active or pending member, and for a
        reasonable period afterwards to maintain accurate community records, unless you request deletion (see
        Section 8). <em>[Flag for legal review: confirm a specific retention period appropriate to your
        jurisdiction and recordkeeping needs.]</em>
      </p>

      <h2>7. Sharing with third parties</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell member data. Data is processed using Supabase (database/authentication hosting) and Netlify
        (website hosting). We do not post to LinkedIn or WhatsApp on your behalf automatically — see the Social
        Sharing section below.
      </p>

      <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Correction:</strong> contact us to correct inaccurate information.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawal of consent:</strong> you may withdraw directory, spotlight, or communications consent at any time; withdrawal unpublishes the relevant content going forward.</li>
        <li><strong>Deletion:</strong> you may request deletion of your personal data, subject to reasonable recordkeeping needs and applicable legal requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Access:</strong> you may request a copy of the personal data we hold about you.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>To exercise any of these rights, contact <a href={`mailto:${siteConfig.contactEmail}`}>{siteConfig.contactEmail}</a>.</p>

      <h2>9. Security</h2>
      <p>
        We use database-level access controls (Row Level Security), restricted administrative access, and
        environment-isolated credentials. No system is perfectly secure; we aim to minimise what is collected and
        exposed publicly by default.
      </p>

      <h2>10. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>This policy may be updated as the website evolves. The version identifier above changes whenever the substantive content changes.</p>

      <h2>11. Social sharing</h2>
      <p>
        Published spotlights, articles, events, and projects include metadata that makes them look good when shared
        on LinkedIn or WhatsApp, but publishing to those platforms is a manual action taken by a person — this
        website does not automatically post on your behalf.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Section>
</BaseLayout>
